<title>USA: Goodyear says could expand plant hours.</title>
<headline>Goodyear says could expand plant hours.</headline>
<dateline>FAYETTEVILLE, N.C. 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goodyear Tire &amp; Rubber Co said late on Thursday that a six-year labour agreement ratified by its unionized employees will allow it to expand operations at its Kelly-Springfield facility.</p>
<p>The contract, which was ratified on Thursday by members of the United Steelworkers of America, will allow that plant to go to a seven-day continuous schedule, the company said.</p>
<p>The increased hours of operation could increase employment by more than 300 people and increase production by about 60,000 tires per week, Goodyear said.</p>
<p>The contract ratification ended a strike of nearly 13,000 U.S. rubber workers that began April 20.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
